1. Purpose

The ARES License allows open, non-commercial research and personal use of this software while protecting the author’s rights to license it commercially for large-scale or for-profit use.

2. Definitions

Software – all source code, models, datasets, weights, and documentation contained in this repository.

Non-Commercial Use – personal, educational, academic, or research use that does not generate direct revenue.

Commercial Use – any use by an organization whose annual gross revenue exceeds USD $500,000, or that integrates the Software into a product, service, or platform offered for sale, subscription, or advertising revenue.

Small Organization – a business or nonprofit with ≤ 5 employees and ≤ USD $500,000 annual revenue.

